// r07_proteinannotator_mt, x02_proteinannotator_mg -- nf-core/proteinannotator 1.1.0
//
// At 1.1.0 the INTERPROSCAN module ignores --interproscan_db and reads the container's
// unpressed sample database, so a real run fails in hmmpress (nf-core/modules#13009);
// the default database URL (5.72-103.0) also does not match the 5.59-91.0 container
// (nf-core/proteinannotator#114). Upstream's workaround (runs/07_proteinannotator/
// README.md): press the 5.59-91.0 release once (`python3 setup.py -f
// interproscan.properties` in the untarred folder) and bind its data/ folder over the
// container's copy. params.interproscan_db is that same data/ folder, so the bind
// follows the metapipeline input instead of a second hard-coded path.
//
// A withName containerOptions replaces any process-wide one from the site profile for
// this process. nf-core/configs m3c sets `containerOptions = '--bind $TMPDIR'` because it
// runs tasks in `scratch = true`, so that bind is repeated here. `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}` is
// expanded by the job's shell; where TMPDIR is unset it binds /tmp, which Singularity
// binds by default anyway.
process {
    withName: '.*:INTERPROSCAN' {
        containerOptions = {
            def target = '/usr/local/share/InterProScan/data'
            workflow.containerEngine in ['singularity', 'apptainer']
                ? "--bind \${TMPDIR:-/tmp} -B ${params.interproscan_db}:${target}"
                : "-v ${params.interproscan_db}:${target}"
        }
    }
}
